# Check out every text file with LF, on every platform. Several tests read
# source files byte-wise and assert on "\n" sequences, and CI runs on
# windows-latest where core.autocrlf=true would otherwise smudge the checkout
# to CRLF. Runtime artifacts that require CRLF (e.g. the generated fmux.cmd
# CLI shim) build their line endings explicitly in code, not from checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Terminal harness recordings are captured PTY byte streams whose CR/LF
# sequences are data — git's text heuristic misclassifies them, so force
# binary to keep normalization from corrupting them.
*.bin binary

# Binary assets.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff2 binary
